{"id":"the-black-riders-and-other-lines","title":"The Black Riders, and Other Lines","author":"Stephen Crane","year":"1895","note":"Stephen Crane's The Black Riders (1895) is poetry as flash and bruise — short lines, hard images, downtown modernism before the manifesto.","minutes":106,"cover":"","coverAlt":"","scenes":[{"id":"s0","title":"Chapter I","place":"Chapter I","reentry":"I","prompt":"What does the poem hold?"},{"id":"s1","title":"Chapter II","place":"Chapter II","reentry":"II","prompt":"What does the poem hold?"},{"id":"s2","title":"Chapter III","place":"Chapter III","reentry":"III","prompt":"What does the poem hold?"},{"id":"s3","title":"Chapter IV","place":"Chapter IV","reentry":"IV","prompt":"What does the poem hold?"},{"id":"s4","title":"Chapter V","place":"Chapter V","reentry":"V","prompt":"What does the poem hold?"},{"id":"s5","title":"Chapter VI","place":"Chapter VI","reentry":"VI","prompt":"What does the poem hold?"},{"id":"s6","title":"Chapter VII","place":"Chapter VII","reentry":"VII","prompt":"What does the poem hold?"},{"id":"s7","title":"Chapter VIII","place":"Chapter VIII","reentry":"VIII","prompt":"What does the poem hold?"},{"id":"s8","title":"Chapter IX","place":"Chapter IX","reentry":"IX","prompt":"What does the poem hold?"},{"id":"s9","title":"Chapter X","place":"Chapter X","reentry":"X","prompt":"What does the poem hold?"}],"breaths":[{"id":"s0-0","sceneId":"s0","text":"I"},{"id":"s0-1","sceneId":"s0","text":"Black Riders came from the sea."},{"id":"s0-2","sceneId":"s0","text":"There was clang and clang of spear and shield,"},{"id":"s0-3","sceneId":"s0","text":"And clash and clash of hoof and heel,"},{"id":"s0-4","sceneId":"s0","text":"Wild shouts and the wave of hair"},{"id":"s0-5","sceneId":"s0","text":"In the rush upon the wind:"},{"id":"s0-6","sceneId":"s0","text":"Thus the ride of Sin."},{"id":"s1-0","sceneId":"s1","text":"II"},{"id":"s1-1","sceneId":"s1","text":"Three little birds in a row"},{"id":"s1-2","sceneId":"s1","text":"Sat musing."},{"id":"s1-3","sceneId":"s1","text":"A man passed near that place."},{"id":"s1-4","sceneId":"s1","text":"Then did the little birds nudge each other."},{"id":"s1-5","sceneId":"s1","text":"They said, \"He thinks he can sing.\""},{"id":"s1-6","sceneId":"s1","text":"They threw back their heads to laugh,"},{"id":"s1-7","sceneId":"s1","text":"With quaint countenances"},{"id":"s1-8","sceneId":"s1","text":"They regarded him."},{"id":"s1-9","sceneId":"s1","text":"They were very curious,"},{"id":"s1-10","sceneId":"s1","text":"Those three little birds in a row."},{"id":"s2-0","sceneId":"s2","text":"III"},{"id":"s2-1","sceneId":"s2","text":"In the desert"},{"id":"s2-2","sceneId":"s2","text":"I saw a creature, naked, bestial,"},{"id":"s2-3","sceneId":"s2","text":"Who, squatting upon the ground,"},{"id":"s2-4","sceneId":"s2","text":"Held his heart in his hands,"},{"id":"s2-5","sceneId":"s2","text":"And ate of it."},{"id":"s2-6","sceneId":"s2","text":"I said, \"Is it good, friend?\""},{"id":"s2-7","sceneId":"s2","text":"\"It is bitter--bitter,\" he answered;"},{"id":"s2-8","sceneId":"s2","text":"\"But I like it"},{"id":"s2-9","sceneId":"s2","text":"Because it is bitter,"},{"id":"s2-10","sceneId":"s2","text":"And because it is my heart.\""},{"id":"s3-0","sceneId":"s3","text":"IV"},{"id":"s3-1","sceneId":"s3","text":"Yes, I have a thousand tongues,"},{"id":"s3-2","sceneId":"s3","text":"And nine and ninety-nine lie."},{"id":"s3-3","sceneId":"s3","text":"Though I strive to use the one,"},{"id":"s3-4","sceneId":"s3","text":"It will make no melody at my will,"},{"id":"s3-5","sceneId":"s3","text":"But is dead in my mouth."},{"id":"s4-0","sceneId":"s4","text":"V"},{"id":"s4-1","sceneId":"s4","text":"Once there came a man"},{"id":"s4-2","sceneId":"s4","text":"Who said,"},{"id":"s4-3","sceneId":"s4","text":"\"Range me all men of the world in rows.\""},{"id":"s4-4","sceneId":"s4","text":"And instantly"},{"id":"s4-5","sceneId":"s4","text":"There was terrific clamor among the people"},{"id":"s4-6","sceneId":"s4","text":"Against being ranged in rows."},{"id":"s4-7","sceneId":"s4","text":"There was a loud quarrel, world-wide."},{"id":"s4-8","sceneId":"s4","text":"It endured for ages;"},{"id":"s4-9","sceneId":"s4","text":"And blood was shed"},{"id":"s4-10","sceneId":"s4","text":"By those who would not stand in rows,"},{"id":"s4-11","sceneId":"s4","text":"And by those who pined to stand in rows,"},{"id":"s4-12","sceneId":"s4","text":"Eventually, the man went to death, weeping."},{"id":"s4-13","sceneId":"s4","text":"And those who staid in bloody scuffle"},{"id":"s4-14","sceneId":"s4","text":"Knew not the great simplicity."},{"id":"s5-0","sceneId":"s5","text":"VI"},{"id":"s5-1","sceneId":"s5","text":"God fashioned the ship of the world carefully"},{"id":"s5-2","sceneId":"s5","text":"With the infinite skill of an All-Master"},{"id":"s5-3","sceneId":"s5","text":"Made He the hull and the sails,"},{"id":"s5-4","sceneId":"s5","text":"Held He the rudder"},{"id":"s5-5","sceneId":"s5","text":"Ready for adjustment."},{"id":"s5-6","sceneId":"s5","text":"Erect stood He, scanning his work proudly."},{"id":"s5-7","sceneId":"s5","text":"Then--at fateful time--a Wrong called,"},{"id":"s5-8","sceneId":"s5","text":"And God turned, heeding."},{"id":"s5-9","sceneId":"s5","text":"Lo, the ship, at this opportunity, slipped slyly,"},{"id":"s5-10","sceneId":"s5","text":"Making cunning noiseless travel down the ways."},{"id":"s5-11","sceneId":"s5","text":"So that, forever rudderless, it went upon the seas"},{"id":"s5-12","sceneId":"s5","text":"Going ridiculous voyages,"},{"id":"s5-13","sceneId":"s5","text":"Making quaint progress,"},{"id":"s5-14","sceneId":"s5","text":"Turning as with serious purpose"},{"id":"s5-15","sceneId":"s5","text":"Before stupid winds."},{"id":"s5-16","sceneId":"s5","text":"And there were many in the sky"},{"id":"s5-17","sceneId":"s5","text":"Who laughed at this thing."},{"id":"s6-0","sceneId":"s6","text":"VII"},{"id":"s6-1","sceneId":"s6","text":"Mystic Shadow, bending near me,"},{"id":"s6-2","sceneId":"s6","text":"Who art thou?"},{"id":"s6-3","sceneId":"s6","text":"Whence come ye?"},{"id":"s6-4","sceneId":"s6","text":"And--tell me--is it fair"},{"id":"s6-5","sceneId":"s6","text":"Or is the truth bitter as eaten fire?"},{"id":"s6-6","sceneId":"s6","text":"Tell me!"},{"id":"s6-7","sceneId":"s6","text":"Fear not that I should quaver,"},{"id":"s6-8","sceneId":"s6","text":"For I dare--I dare."},{"id":"s6-9","sceneId":"s6","text":"Then, tell me!"},{"id":"s7-0","sceneId":"s7","text":"VIII"},{"id":"s7-1","sceneId":"s7","text":"I looked here;"},{"id":"s7-2","sceneId":"s7","text":"I looked there;"},{"id":"s7-3","sceneId":"s7","text":"Nowhere could I see my love."},{"id":"s7-4","sceneId":"s7","text":"And--this time--"},{"id":"s7-5","sceneId":"s7","text":"She was in my heart."},{"id":"s7-6","sceneId":"s7","text":"Truly, then, I have no complaint,"},{"id":"s7-7","sceneId":"s7","text":"For though she be fair and fairer,"},{"id":"s7-8","sceneId":"s7","text":"She is none so fair as she"},{"id":"s7-9","sceneId":"s7","text":"In my heart."},{"id":"s8-0","sceneId":"s8","text":"IX"},{"id":"s8-1","sceneId":"s8","text":"I stood upon a high place,"},{"id":"s8-2","sceneId":"s8","text":"And saw, below, many devils"},{"id":"s8-3","sceneId":"s8","text":"Running, leaping,"},{"id":"s8-4","sceneId":"s8","text":"And carousing in sin."},{"id":"s8-5","sceneId":"s8","text":"One looked up, grinning,"},{"id":"s8-6","sceneId":"s8","text":"And said, \"Comrade!  Brother!\""},{"id":"s9-0","sceneId":"s9","text":"X"}]}